fix: water feature distribution bug + add water diversity brute-force test

TerrainAssigner water feature selection for inter-cluster trails used
`roll / 100UL % 10UL` (range 0-9) with thresholds written for 0-99:
- Short inter-cluster: `< 85` always true for 0-9, Creek never appeared
- Long inter-cluster: `< 85` always true, Spring and River never appeared
- WaterFeature.River never appeared on any generated map

Fix: use `roll / 100UL % 100UL` (range 0-99) for all water branches,
matching the threshold intent and using a different roll slice than
terrain/risk for independence. Intra-cluster water also updated for
consistency (was correct but used a different slice pattern).

Added BruteForce_WaterDiversity_AllTypesAppear test collecting
WaterFeature counts across all 4224 combinations. River gets a 1%
floor (only ~5% of long inter-cluster trails, which are a subset).

Caught by final code review (issue #1 and #2).

